            "review_title": "Review at Seoul BBQ",
            "review_text": "Greg D\nWhitehorse40 contributions\n0\nAmazing food, service, and prices!\nNov 2019 • Friends\nThis place was so good I had to create a listing on trip advisor just so I could leave them a review!\n\nAt first we thought it was a little pricey, but the seafood platter looked good so we ordered that. The waitress tried to tell us something but it was hard to uderstand her, I thought she was telling us everything on the page was the same price. I was like \"ok.\"\n\nThey start bringing us the dishes and its beef and pork... then a noodle salad... then the seafood... then a regular salad... then more seafood... then oysters! I was like, \"Oh, god, I thnk I just ordred the whole damn page!\" But we were good sports and we ate it all. Then they bring us more seafood, more oysters, and we were stuffed. I was starting to think about how big this bill was going to be. Would have been $200+ back home. \n\nThis whole time its a young waiter cooking all the food on the BBQ for us. He opens the menu and gestures to some beef, but we delined and gestured that we were full. He turned off the BBQ (its propaine assisted charcoal! Yum!) \n\nSo now it was time for the damages. A whole menu page of seafood and 6 beers... \n\n800k?! That's it? Oh? The whole page WAS the meal! Wow! What a deal.\n\nGreat service, great food, great prices. \n\nWill definitely be back when I'm really hungry.\nRead more\nWritten November 7, 2019",
